.th DEVNM VIII 5/31/77
.sh NAME
devnm \*- device name
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd /etc/devnm
[argument(s)...]
.sh DESCRIPTION
Devnm identifies the special file
.it special
(e.g.,  "/dev/rp2"),
associated with the mounted file system where the argument name resides.
.s3
Devnm prints the unqualified path name of the special file
followed by the argument name.
.s3
Example:
.in +5
/etc/devnm /unix
.br
rp2 /unix
.in -5
.sh FILES
/dev/rf?, /dev/rk?, /dev/rp?
